.TH __NAME__ 1 __NAME__\-VERSION
.SH NAME
__NAME__ \- pick a line interactively
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B __NAME__
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B __NAME__
reads lines from standard input and draws them as a list on
.IR /dev/tty .
Typing filters the list; the chosen line is printed on standard output.
Because only the result goes to standard output,
.B __NAME__
works in any pipeline, terminal or tmux pane.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
print version information to standard output, then exit.
.SH USAGE
.TP
.I text
filter the list (case-insensitive substring).
.TP
.BR Up ", " Ctrl\-p
move the selection up.
.TP
.BR Down ", " Ctrl\-n
move the selection down.
.TP
.B Backspace
delete the last filter character.
.TP
.B Enter
print the selected line and exit.
.TP
.BR Esc ", " Ctrl\-c
cancel.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
when non-empty, no colours are drawn; the selection is shown in reverse video.
.TP
.B TERM
.B dumb
makes
.B __NAME__
exit with an error, as it cannot draw.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
A line was picked.
.TP
1
Cancelled, no input, or an error.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
git branch \-\-format='%(refname:short)' | __NAME__ | xargs git switch
.EE
